{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>tet – we are justified.</b> A tav of the hitpa'el in place of a tzadi, on account of the tzadi." "<b>Elohim has found.</b> By way of parable: the iniquity was ours, and it was as though it was forgotten and gone, and today it is found." "Or the meaning of עון עבדיך may be like גדול עוני מנשוא (Genesis 4:13)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {0 "He reads נצטדק as a hitpa'el form; the tet (of the hitpa'el prefix) appears in place of the expected tzadi, because the root contains a tzadi (צדק)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:01.131230496Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}